# The auxiliary transceiver's reset and the six LEDs of a Great Scott
# Gadgets Cynthion r1.4 — the two things `quiesce.v` drives, and nothing
# else.
#
# `J13` is Great Scott Gadgets' own, from
# `cynthion/python/src/gateware/platform/cynthion_r1_4.py`:
#
#     ULPIResource("aux_phy", 0,
#         data="F16 G15 G16 H15 J15 J16 K15 K16", clk="D16", clk_dir='o',
#         dir="E16", nxt="F15", stp="E15", rst="J13", rst_invert=True,
#         attrs=Attrs(IO_TYPE="LVCMOS33", SLEWRATE="FAST")),
#
# `rst_invert=True` says the ball is active low, which is the transceiver's
# own reset input, so `quiesce.v` drives a literal zero and nothing
# inverts. Project Trellis' `iodb.json` puts `J13` at row 17, column 72,
# PIO C — the die's right edge, where the rest of that resource lives.
#
# The LEDs are the same six, in the same order, as `leds.rcf`:
#
#     *LEDResources(pins="E13 C13 B14 A15 D12 C11",
#                   attrs=Attrs(IO_TYPE="LVCMOS33"), invert=True),
#
# so `led5_n` is `C11`, the end of the row nearest the `USER` button, and it
# is the only one this design lights. All six are constrained and driven,
# because a dark LED that is being held dark says more than a dark LED that
# nothing is connected to.
#
# **No `-pullup` on `J13`.** The far end of that net is a transceiver's
# reset input; an internal pull would be fighting the board. `configure_io`
# writes `PULLMODE = NONE`, which is what the platform file's attributes ask
# for too.
#
# `SLEWRATE="FAST"` is an attribute of that resource this backend does not
# write; see "What remains" in `docs/fpga-trellis.md`. It is an edge rate,
# and this design has no edges.
#
# The eight data balls, `dir`, `nxt`, `stp` and the interface clock are
# deliberately absent. `quiesce.v`'s header says why for each.

set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 ulpi_rst_n J13

set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led0_n E13
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led1_n C13
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led2_n B14
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led3_n A15
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led4_n D12
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led5_n C11
